{"title":"Career Roadmap: Space Designer","role":"Space Designer","summary":"A Space Designer creates functional, engaging, and visually coherent environments by combining spatial planning, architecture, interiors, user experience, materials, lighting, circulation, and technology.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Arch (Bachelor of Architecture)","Course":"Interior Architecture & Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Space Designer creates functional, engaging, and visually coherent environments by combining spatial planning, architecture, interiors, user experience, materials, lighting, circulation, and technology."},{"type":"p","text":"The role can span:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Residential spaces"},{"text":"Offices and workplaces"},{"text":"Retail stores"},{"text":"Hospitality"},{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"Educational environments"},{"text":"Exhibitions"},{"text":"Cultural spaces"},{"text":"Public interiors"},{"text":"Experiential and branded environments"},{"text":"A strong Space Designer goes beyond decoration. The focus is on how people move through, interact with, and experience a space."}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Spatial design, interior architecture, CAD/BIM, visualization, materials and design internships"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Space Designer, Interior Architect, Spatial Designer, Workplace/Retail Designer"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior Space Designer, Design Lead, Experience Design Lead, Project Design Manager"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Design Director, Creative Director, Principal Designer, Studio Founder"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Arch","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Spatial Design Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Architectural design"},{"text":"Spatial thinking"},{"text":"Proportion and scale"},{"text":"Human dimensions"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Circulation"},{"text":"Basic interior design"},{"text":"Architectural representation"},{"text":"Freehand sketching"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to understand the relationship between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["People","Space","Function","Movement"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Interior Architecture"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Space planning"},{"text":"Furniture planning"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Interior construction"},{"text":"Joinery"},{"text":"Flooring"},{"text":"Ceilings"},{"text":"Doors and partitions"},{"text":"Lighting fundamentals"},{"text":"Color and texture"},{"text":"Start developing detailed interior drawings."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Digital Spatial Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"SketchUp"},{"text":"Revit"},{"text":"Rhino"},{"text":"3D modelling"},{"text":"Rendering"},{"text":"Visualization"},{"text":"BIM"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Enscape"},{"text":"V-Ray"},{"text":"Twinmotion"},{"text":"D5 Render"},{"text":"Develop the ability to communicate a spatial concept through both 2D documentation and 3D visualization."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Experience + Professional Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Workplace design"},{"text":"Retail design"},{"text":"Hospitality"},{"text":"Healthcare interiors"},{"text":"Exhibition design"},{"text":"Branding in physical spaces"},{"text":"Lighting design"},{"text":"Acoustics"},{"text":"Building services"},{"text":"Material specifications"},{"text":"BOQ"},{"text":"Vendor coordination"},{"text":"Site execution"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 5 — Specialization / Thesis"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose a project where space and user experience are central."},{"type":"p","text":"Possible topics:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Future workplace"},{"text":"Experience-driven retail"},{"text":"Sustainable hospitality"},{"text":"Healthcare environment"},{"text":"Cultural center"},{"text":"Museum"},{"text":"Co-working space"},{"text":"Learning environment"},{"text":"Airport lounge"},{"text":"Exhibition and experience center"},{"text":"Adaptive-reuse interior"}]}]},{"heading":"Core Technical Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"A. Spatial Planning"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Space programming"},{"text":"Zoning"},{"text":"Adjacency planning"},{"text":"Circulation"},{"text":"Furniture layout"},{"text":"Human scale"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Spatial hierarchy"},{"text":"Wayfinding"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong space designer should be able to answer:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Who uses the space?","What do they need?","How do they move?","What should they experience?"]},{"type":"h","text":"B. Ergonomics"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anthropometrics"},{"text":"Furniture dimensions"},{"text":"Workstation ergonomics"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Universal design"},{"text":"Reach ranges"},{"text":"Clearances"},{"text":"Circulation widths"}]},{"type":"h","text":"C. Materials"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wood"},{"text":"Stone"},{"text":"Metal"},{"text":"Glass"},{"text":"Concrete"},{"text":"Ceramics"},{"text":"Fabrics"},{"text":"Acoustic materials"},{"text":"Recycled materials"},{"text":"Low-VOC finishes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how materials affect:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Appearance"},{"text":"Durability"},{"text":"Acoustics"},{"text":"Maintenance"},{"text":"Cost"},{"text":"Sustainability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"D. Lighting"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Natural lighting"},{"text":"Ambient lighting"},{"text":"Task lighting"},{"text":"Accent lighting"},{"text":"Color temperature"},{"text":"Glare"},{"text":"Lighting layers"},{"text":"Daylight integration"},{"text":"Lighting should be treated as a spatial design element, not simply an electrical requirement."}]},{"type":"h","text":"E. Acoustics"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sound absorption"},{"text":"Sound reflection"},{"text":"Reverberation"},{"text":"Acoustic zoning"},{"text":"Noise control"},{"text":"Workplace acoustics"},{"text":"Hospitality acoustics"}]}]},{"heading":"Experience & Spatial Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A modern Space Designer should understand experience design."},{"type":"p","text":"Consider:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arrival experience"},{"text":"Wayfinding"},{"text":"Visual hierarchy"},{"text":"Branding"},{"text":"Sensory experience"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Sound"},{"text":"Materiality"},{"text":"Digital interaction"},{"text":"User psychology"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For commercial spaces:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Brand","Space","Customer Journey","Experience"]}]},{"heading":"Tools & Software","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Essential"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"Revit"},{"text":"SketchUp"},{"text":"Adobe Photoshop"},{"text":"Adobe Illustrator"},{"text":"Microsoft Excel"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rhino"},{"text":"Grasshopper"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Visualization"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Enscape"},{"text":"V-Ray"},{"text":"Twinmotion"},{"text":"D5 Render"},{"text":"Lumion"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Presentation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"InDesign"},{"text":"PowerPoint"},{"text":"Figma"}]},{"type":"h","text":"BIM"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Revit"},{"text":"Navisworks"},{"text":"A strong portfolio should demonstrate both design thinking and technical documentation."}]}]},{"heading":"Five Recommended UG Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Future Workplace"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a modern workplace with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Collaboration areas"},{"text":"Focus zones"},{"text":"Meeting spaces"},{"text":"Informal spaces"},{"text":"Wellness areas"},{"text":"Flexible furniture"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Demonstrate:"},{"type":"flow","items":["User Research","Space Program","Zoning","Circulation","Design","Visualization"]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Experiential Retail Store"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a retail environment around a brand."},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Customer journey"},{"text":"Product display"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Branding"},{"text":"Wayfinding"},{"text":"Checkout"},{"text":"Back-of-house"},{"text":"Show how the physical environment communicates the brand."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Boutique Hospitality Space"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a boutique hotel, café, restaurant, or lounge."},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arrival"},{"text":"Circulation"},{"text":"Atmosphere"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Acoustics"},{"text":"Guest experience"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Healthcare Interior"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a patient-centered healthcare environment."},{"type":"p","text":"Consider:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Wayfinding"},{"text":"Privacy"},{"text":"Infection-control principles"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Acoustics"},{"text":"Patient comfort"},{"text":"Staff circulation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Adaptive-Reuse Cultural Space"},{"type":"p","text":"Transform an existing building into:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gallery"},{"text":"Museum"},{"text":"Cultural center"},{"text":"Creative studio"},{"text":"Exhibition space"},{"text":"Demonstrate how existing architectural elements can be integrated into a new spatial experience."}]}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","tex